  "scope": "Full original Hermitian/trace-dual lattice constructors and quantitative DataX endpoints on supplied principal charts; all twelve claims and original conditional boundary.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Original Hermitian coordinates and sign",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Read all twelve mathematical proofs. The original perfect alternating datum is torsion-free, its rationalization has the supplied E-rank, and nondegeneracy of the field trace uniquely reconstructs the left-linear skew-Hermitian form. Dividing by the actual imaginary xi gives the stated Hermitian form and original lattice injection; the chart trace form uses the explicitly recorded minus sign."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Nonprincipal ideal duality and exact different",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Verified both ideal-valued dual identities by finite invertible-ideal decompositions, without assuming that a lattice or ideal has one generator. The trace-dual lattice is ((xi)D_E)^(-1)L-sharp; integral perfection gives L-sharp=(xi)D_E L. The actual A^(-1)Lambda is therefore self-dual under the original principal product identity."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Complete DataX constructor",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Compared every original DataX field and the whole exists_dataX_of_perfect_traceForm endpoint. Both positive denominator witnesses, k0=2k and its bounds, actual lattice inclusions, unchanged Data and the original positive-modulus congruence clause are supplied. No pre-existing scalar, matrix, metric or group is replaced."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Original uniformization trace pairing",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Read literal IsUnf fields77–95 and the original trace-perfection endpoint. Its actual integral lattice equivalence transports both integrality and surjectivity onto the Z-dual for each supplied component. Existence of IsUnf is retained."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Actual host ideal and scalar",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The quadratic integer-ring and trace-dual calculations give D_K=(sqrt(-d)); the split/inert/ramified prime calculations give C*conj(C)=(Norm C). Together with the actual half-different these prove (xi_H)A*conj(A)*D_E=1. The scalar xi_H=-1/(Norm(C)*sqrt(-d)) and absolute value 1/(Norm(C)*sqrt(d)) match original DataHost and ModelDataX."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Quantitative denominators and logarithms",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "NA=Norm_E(b) and NC=Norm_K(ccK) lie in the exact required ideals and work for every original component. Norms of conjugate ideals agree, so NA^2<=abs(discriminant E), giving log NA<=f_E log rd(E) with the exact factor one-half. The source SupBoundPageRows fourth conjunct supplies the NC logarithmic bound."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Literal all-row endpoints and retained boundary",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Compared exists_dataX_of_hasPrinc, both GamAt predicates, the core DataX model endpoint and DataXOfModelSt. All original rows, good embeddings, components, levels and later size/weight quantifiers are preserved. Equal absolute values of purely imaginary scalars at one injective embedding give xi=plus/minus xi_H, sufficient for the exact ideal identity. IsUnf, HasPrinc/GamAt, LawsCore, common uniformization and the separate theta/Gaussian/short-rule/ramified-jet producers remain explicit. No selected whole leaf is closed."
    }
